hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1399.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from Zaynab bint Abi Salama from Umm Salama"
"1399.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from Zaynab bint Abi Salama from Umm Salama"
"1400.1","Malik related to me from Yahya ibn Said from Said ibn al-Musayyab that Umar ibn al-Khattab had a dispute brought to him between a muslim and a jew. Umar saw that the right belonged to the jew and decided in his favour. The jew said to him"
"1400.2","Malik related to me from Yahya ibn Said from Said ibn al-Musayyab that Umar ibn al-Khattab had a dispute brought to him between a muslim and a jew. Umar saw that the right belonged to the jew and decided in his favour. The jew said to him"
"1401.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm from his father from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Uthman from Abu Amra al-Ansari from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani that the Messenger of Allah"
"1401.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm from his father from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Uthman from Abu Amra al-Ansari from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani that the Messenger of Allah"
"1402.1",""
"1402.2","Malik related to me that Rabia ibn Abi Abd ar-Rahman said"
"1403.1","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Rabi'ah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, from Hanzalah."
"1403.2","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Rabi'ah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, from Hanzalah ibn Qays al-Zurayqi, from Rafi' ibn Khadij, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, forbade the renting of farmland. Hanzalah said: \"So I asked Rafi' ibn Khadij, 'What about with gold and silver?' He said: 'As for with gold and silver, there is no harm in it.'\""
"1404.1","Yahya said from Malik that he heard from Sulayman ibn Yasar and others that when they were asked whether the testimony of a man flogged for a hadd crime was permitted"
"1404.2","Yahya said from Malik that he heard from Sulayman ibn Yasar and others that when they were asked whether the testimony of a man flogged for a hadd crime was permitted"
"1405.1","And Yahya narrated to me, from Malik, from Yunus bin Yusuf, from Sa'id bin Al-Musayyab, that Umar bin Al-Khattab passed by Hatib bin Abi Balta'ah while he was selling his raisins in the market. Umar bin Al-Khattab said to him: \"Either you increase the price, or you remove yourself from our market.\""
"1405.2","And Malik narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, that he asked Salim bin Abdullah bin Umar about renting out farms. He said: \"There is no harm in it for gold and silver.\" Ibn Shihab said: \"So I said to him: What do you think about the hadith that is mentioned from Rafi' bin Khadij?\" He said: \"Rafi' exaggerated. If I had a farm, I would rent it out.\""
"1406.1",""
"1406.2",""
"1407.1","From Malik from Abu'z-Zinad that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz wrote to Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn al-Khattab who was the governor of Kufa"
"1407.2","From Malik from Abu'z-Zinad that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz wrote to Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn al-Khattab who was the governor of Kufa"
"1408.1","Malik related to me that he heard that Abu Salama ibn Abd ar- Rahman and Sulayman ibn Yasar were both asked"
"1408.2","Malik related to me that he heard that Abu Salama ibn Abd ar- Rahman and Sulayman ibn Yasar were both asked"
"1409.1","Yahya said that Malik spoke about a man who died and had a debt owing to him and there was one witness"
"1409.2","Yahya said that Malik spoke about a man who died and had a debt owing to him and there was one witness"
"1410.1",""
"1410.2",""
"1411.1",""
"1411.2",""
"1412.1","Malik related to me from al-Ala ibn Abd ar-Rahman from Mabad ibn Kab as-Salami from his brother Abdullah ibn Kab ibn Malik al-Ansari from Abu Umama that the Messenger of Allah"
"1412.2","Malik related to me from al-Ala ibn Abd ar-Rahman from Mabad ibn Kab as-Salami from his brother Abdullah ibn Kab ibn Malik al-Ansari from Abu Umama that the Messenger of Allah"
"1413.1","Yahya said that Malik had said from Da'ud ibn al-Husayn that he heard Abu Ghatafan ibn Tarif al-Muriyi say"
"1413.2","Yahya said that Malik had said from Da'ud ibn al-Husayn that he heard Abu Ghatafan ibn Tarif al-Muriyi say"
"1414.1",""
"1414.2",""
"1415.1",""
"1415.2",""
"1416.1","And Yahya narrated to me, from Malik, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Bakr bin Abdur Rahman bin Al-Harith bin Hisham, from Abu Mas'ud Al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) prohibited the price of a dog, the dowry of a prostitute, and the fee of a soothsayer. Meaning by the dowry of a prostitute what a woman is given for fornication, and the fee of a soothsayer is his bribe and what is given for soothsaying."
"1416.2","And Malik narrated to me that it reached him that Umar bin Al-Khattab said: \"The testimony of an opponent or someone suspected is not permissible.\""
"1417.1","Malik related to me from Abd ar-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Qari that his father said"
"1417.2","Malik related to me from Abd ar-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Qari that his father said"
"1418.1",""
"1418.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih as- Samman from his father from Abu Hurayra that Sad ibn Ubada said to the Messenger of Allah"
"1419.1","Malik related to me from Yahya ibn Said from Said ibn al-Musayyab that a Syrian man called Ibn Khaybari found a man with his wife and killed him"
"1419.2","Malik related to me from Yahya ibn Said from Said ibn al-Musayyab that a Syrian man called Ibn Khaybari found a man with his wife and killed him"
"1420.1","Yahya said that Malik related from Ibn Shihab that Sunayn Abi Jamila"
"1420.2","Yahya said that Malik related from Ibn Shihab that Sunayn Abi Jamila"
"1421.1","Yahya said from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Urwa ibn az-Zubayr that A'isha"
"1421.2","Yahya said from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Urwa ibn az-Zubayr that A'isha"
"1422.1","Malik related to me from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Hadi from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith at-Taymi from Sulayman ibn Yasar from Abdullah ibn Abi Umayya that a woman's husband died"
"1422.2","Malik related to me from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Hadi from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith at-Taymi from Sulayman ibn Yasar from Abdullah ibn Abi Umayya that a woman's husband died"
"1423.1","Malik related to me from Yahya ibn Said from Sulayman ibn Yasar that Umar ibn al-Khattab used to attach the children of the Jahiliyya to whoever claimed them in Islam. Two men came and each of them claimed a woman's child. Umar ibn al-Khattab summoned a person who scrutinized features and he looked at them. The scrutinizer said"
"1423.2","Malik related to me from Yahya ibn Said from Sulayman ibn Yasar that Umar ibn al-Khattab used to attach the children of the Jahiliyya to whoever claimed them in Islam. Two men came and each of them claimed a woman's child. Umar ibn al-Khattab summoned a person who scrutinized features and he looked at them. The scrutinizer said"
"1424.1","Malik related to me that he had heard that Umar ibn al-Khattab or Uthman ibn Affan gave a judgement about a slave woman who misled a man about herself and said that she was free. He married her and she bore children. It was decided that he should ransom his children with their like of slaves. Yahya said that he heard Malik say"
"1424.2","Malik related to me that he had heard that Umar ibn al-Khattab or Uthman ibn Affan gave a judgement about a slave woman who misled a man about herself and said that she was free. He married her and she bore children. It was decided that he should ransom his children with their like of slaves. Yahya said that he heard Malik say"
"1425.1","Malik narrated to me, from Al-Ala' ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ma'bad ibn Ka'b al-Silmi..."
"1425.2","Malik narrated to me, from Al-Ala' ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ma'bad ibn Ka'b al-Silmi, from his brother, Abdullah ibn Ka'b ibn Malik al-Ansari, from Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever seizes the right of a Muslim by his oath, Allah has forbidden Paradise for him and made the Fire obligatory for him.\" They said: \"Even if it is something small, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"Even if it is a twig of Arak, even if it is a twig of Arak, even if it is a twig of Arak.\" He said this three times."
"1426.1","Malik related to me from Nafi that Safiyya bint Abi Ubayd informed him that Umar ibn al-Khattab said"
"1426.2","Malik related to me from Nafi that Safiyya bint Abi Ubayd informed him that Umar ibn al-Khattab said"
"1427.1","Yahya related from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that the Messenger of Allah"
"1427.2","Yahya related from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that the Messenger of Allah"
"1428.1","Malik related to me from Ibn Shihab from Salim ibn Abdullah from his father that Umar ibn al-Khattab said"
"1428.2","Malik related to me from Ibn Shihab from Salim ibn Abdullah from his father that Umar ibn al-Khattab said"
"1429.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm that he heard that the Messenger of Allah"
"1429.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm that he heard that the Messenger of Allah"
"1430.1","Malik related to me from Abu'z-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"1430.2","Malik related to me from Abu'z-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"1431.1","Malik related to me from Abu'r-Rijal Muhammad ibn Abd ar-Rahman from his mother Amra bint Abd ar-Rahman that she informed him that the Messenger of Allah"
"1431.2","Malik related to me from Abu'r-Rijal Muhammad ibn Abd ar-Rahman from his mother Amra bint Abd ar-Rahman that she informed him that the Messenger of Allah"
"1432.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Amr ibn Yahya al-Mazini from his father that the Messenger of Allah"
"1432.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Amr ibn Yahya al-Mazini from his father that the Messenger of Allah"
"1433.1",""
"1433.2","Malik related to me from Ibn Shihab from al-Araj from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"1434.1","Malik related to me from Amr ibn Yahya al-Mazini from his father that ad-Dahhak ibn Khalifa watered his irrigation ditch from a large source of water. He wanted to have it pass through the land of Muhammad ibn Maslama"
"1434.2","Malik related to me from Amr ibn Yahya al-Mazini from his father that ad-Dahhak ibn Khalifa watered his irrigation ditch from a large source of water. He wanted to have it pass through the land of Muhammad ibn Maslama"
"1435.1","Malik related to me from Amr ibn Yahya al-Mazini that his father said"
"1435.2","Malik related to me from Amr ibn Yahya al-Mazini that his father said"
"1436.1","Yahya related to me from Malik that Thawr ibn Zayd ad-Dili said"
"1436.2","Yahya related to me from Malik that Thawr ibn Zayd ad-Dili said"
"1437.1","Yahya said that he heard Malik speak about a man who died and left properties in Aliya and Safila (outlying districts of Madina). He said"
"1437.2","Yahya said that he heard Malik speak about a man who died and left properties in Aliya and Safila (outlying districts of Madina). He said"
"1438.1","Malik related to me from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from Yahya ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Hatib that some slaves of Hatib stole a she-camel belonging to a man from the Muzayna tribe and they slaughtered it. The case was brought before Umar ibn al-Khattab"
"1438.2","Malik related to me from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from Yahya ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Hatib that some slaves of Hatib stole a she-camel belonging to a man from the Muzayna tribe and they slaughtered it. The case was brought before Umar ibn al-Khattab"
"1439.1","Yahya narrated to me, from Malik, that it reached him that Umar ibn al-Khattab said regarding a man who advanced food to another man on the condition that he would deliver it in another city, that Umar ibn al-Khattab disliked this and said: \"Then where is the carrying?\" meaning its carriage."
"1439.2","Malik narrated to me, from Nafi', from Safiyyah bint Abi Ubayd, that she informed him that Umar ibn al-Khattab said: \"What is the matter with men who have intercourse with their slave women and then let them go out? No slave woman comes to me whose master admits to having had intercourse with her, except that I have joined her child to him. So send them away afterwards, or keep them.\""
"1440.1","Malik related to me from Ibn Shihab from Urwa ibn az-Zubayr that A'isha"
"1440.2","Malik related to me from Ibn Shihab from Urwa ibn az-Zubayr that A'isha"
"1441.1","Malik related to me from Ibn Shihab from Urwa ibn az-Zubayr from Abd ar-Rahman ibn Abd al-Qari that Umar ibn al-Khattab said"
"1441.2","Malik related to me from Ibn Shihab from Urwa ibn az-Zubayr from Abd ar-Rahman ibn Abd al-Qari that Umar ibn al-Khattab said"
"1442.1",""
"1442.2","Yahya narrated to me, from Malik, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, that it reached him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said concerning the floodwaters of Mahzoor and Muzaynab: \"It is held back until the ankles, then the upper part is sent upon the lower part.\""
"1443.1","Yahya narrated to me, from Malik, from Nafi, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Let not one of you sell upon the sale of another.\""
"1443.2","Yahya narrated to me, from Malik, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, that it reached him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Excess water shall not be withheld to prevent fodder.\""
"1444.1","Malik related to me from Yahya ibn Said that Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim ibn Muhammad heard Makhul ad-Dimashqi ask al-Qasim ibn Muhammad about the life pension and what people said about it. Al- Qasim ibn Muhammad said"
"1444.2","Malik related to me from Yahya ibn Said that Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim ibn Muhammad heard Makhul ad-Dimashqi ask al-Qasim ibn Muhammad about the life pension and what people said about it. Al- Qasim ibn Muhammad said"
"1445.1","Malik related to me from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar inherited the house of Hafsa bint Umar. He said"
"1445.2","Malik related to me from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar inherited the house of Hafsa bint Umar. He said"
"1446.1","Malik related to me from Rabia ibn Abi Abd ar-Rahman from Yazid"
"1446.2","Malik related to me from Rabia ibn Abi Abd ar-Rahman from Yazid"
"1447.1","Malik related to me from Ayyub ibn Musa from Muawiya ibn Abdullah ibn Badr al-Juhani that his father informed him that he stopped with a people on the way to Syria and he found a purse which had eighty dinars in it. He mentioned that to Umar ibn al-Khattab. Umar said to him"
"1447.2","Malik related to me from Ayyub ibn Musa from Muawiya ibn Abdullah ibn Badr al-Juhani that his father informed him that he stopped with a people on the way to Syria and he found a purse which had eighty dinars in it. He mentioned that to Umar ibn al-Khattab. Umar said to him"
"1448.1","Malik related to me from Nafi that a man found something and went to Abdullah ibn Umar and said to him"
"1448.2","Malik related to me from Nafi that a man found something and went to Abdullah ibn Umar and said to him"
"1449.1","Malik narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, that he asked him about a man who rents a beast of burden and then rents it out for more than he rented it for. He said: \"There is no harm in that.\""
"1449.2","Yahya narrated to me, from Malik, from Thurayh bin Zayd al-Dili, that he said: It has reached me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Any house or land that was divided in the Jahiliyyah, then it is according to the division of the Jahiliyyah. And any house or land that Islam reached and it was not divided, then it is according to the division of Islam.\""
"1450.1","Malik related to me from Yahya ibn Said from Said ibn al-Musayyab that Umar ibn al-Khattab said while he was leaning his back against the Kaba"
"1450.2","Malik related to me from Yahya ibn Said from Said ibn al-Musayyab that Umar ibn al-Khattab said while he was leaning his back against the Kaba"
"1451.1","Malik narrated to me, from al-Ala' bin Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from his grandfather, that Uthman bin Affan gave him wealth as a qirad (a type of partnership) to work with, on the condition that the profit would be between them."
"1451.2","Malik narrated to me, from Hisham bin Urwah, from his father, from Yahya bin Abd al-Rahman bin Hatib, that some slaves of Hatib stole a she-camel belonging to a man from Muzaynah. They slaughtered it. This was brought to Umar bin al-Khattab, and Umar ordered Kathir bin al-Salt to cut off their hands. Then Umar said: \"I think you are starving them.\" Then Umar said: \"By Allah, I will make you pay a fine that will be difficult for you.\" Then he said to the Muzani: \"What was the price of your she-camel?\" The Muzani said: \"By Allah, I used to prevent it from being sold for less than four hundred dirhams.\" Umar said: \"Give him eight hundred dirhams.\""
"1452.1","Malik related to me from Said ibn Amr Shurahbil ibn Said ibn Sad ibn Ubada from his father that his father said"
"1452.2","Malik related to me from Said ibn Amr Shurahbil ibn Said ibn Sad ibn Ubada from his father that his father said"
"1453.1","Malik related to me from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from A'isha"
"1453.2","Malik related to me from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from A'isha"
"1454.1","Malik related to me that he heard that a man of the Ansar from the tribe of Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj"
"1454.2","Malik related to me that he heard that a man of the Ansar from the tribe of Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj"
